- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_dissipate.html
- Summary (EN): Gradually reduces the values of a VDB so that smoke or other volume data fades over time. Drives values toward a goal value (usually zero). An optional control field can limit where dissipation happens.
- Résumé (FR) : Pyro Dissipate réduit progressivement les valeurs d'un VDB pour que la fumée s'estompe, avec un champ de contrôle optionnel pour limiter la zone touchée.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: Float or Vector VDB driven toward a goal value", "control (optional): Float or Vector VDB used as a control field; a Vector VDB contributes its length"]

- Key parameters: ["Mode: Dissipation Rate (percentage lost per second), Subtraction Rate (fixed amount lost per second), Lifespan (time for one unit to be lost), Half-Life (time for half the amount to be lost)", "Goal Value: value the field cools toward, usually zero", "Goal Tolerance: when enabled, values within this range of the goal are pushed all the way to the Goal Value", "Control Volume, Control Range, Use Ramp, Control Ramp: mask the effect with the control field and remap its values to 0-1", "Axis Mask, Axis Direction, Axis Range, Use Ramp, Axis Control Ramp: limit the effect along a world-space axis", "Minimum Limit / Maximum Limit: clamp the output VDB values"]

- Caveats: ["Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education", "The Control Range description refers to a Scale multiplier, but no Scale parameter is listed on the page, so its exact location is unclear"]

